# Assessment engine

One attempt per student. Auto-grade only. Third integrity strike →
the third event on the same question makes that question worth zero while the
attempt continues. `integrity_stopped` is legacy-only. Full review after submit.
Full cards on the **day page**.

## Course overview chip

On `c/[slug]/page.tsx`, name the assessment kind (`Pre-assessment` / `Quiz` /
`Post-assessment`). Only use `"N assessments"` when a day has more than one.
Never label a pre/post as “1 quiz”.

## Authoring

- Prompt: `public/assessment-authoring-prompt.md`
- Validate: `src/lib/assessment-schema.ts` (`sdaia-assessment/v1`) — most rules
  are hard errors; word-cue style checks stay warnings
- Import confirms file day + duration against the selected assessment
- Import/edit RPCs refuse if attempts exist → Reset attempts first

## Runtime

- Student route: `/quiz/[assessmentId]` under `(quiz)` layout
- Actions: `src/app/actions/quiz.ts` → RPCs
- Never return answer keys mid-attempt; options have no correctness column

## After schema/RPC changes

Re-run the checklist in `docs/ASSESSMENTS.md`, regenerate `src/lib/types.ts`,
and call `revalidateCourseContent` from question mutations.
